+# v1.2.63 - a split is merged after Redo part
+
+- **Asked:** "when the video processing stops, stating it is not visible, and you redo it, after redo the merge doesn't happen".
+- **Causes found in 1.2.62 (PhoenixViewModel.kt):**
+  - History kept the newest **50** entries. The parts of a split, the jobs after them and the redone part pushed the oldest
+    parts of the same video out of History; the merge then waited for parts it could no longer see ("Merge waits for all n
+    parts").
+  - The automatic merge after a part finished merged only when this part's split was the **first** mergeable one in History.
+    Any other split left complete but unmerged (its merge had failed once, or Auto-merge was off then) blocked it.
+  - A split merged once was never merged again, and a new merge would have been saved under the old file name - which hands
+    back the **old** merged video.
+  - **Refresh** removed a finished part whose file had been moved or deleted, so its card and its Redo part button vanished.
+  - At start the app watched the old job of a replaced part again; it came back as "Lost" (or, had the Space kept it, as a
+    second copy of that part).
+- **Changes:**
+  - `SplitLogic.kt` (new, plain Kotlin): for each part number the newest finished entry is joined (a redone part replaces the
+    lost one; two finished copies are joined once); a split is merged again when a part was redone after its merge, as a new
+    file (`Phoenix_merged_<group>_2.mp4`); History keeps the newest 50 entries **and every entry of a split not merged yet**
+    (at most 300).
+  - The automatic merge after a part finishes checks that part's own split.
+  - Before joining, every part's file is checked. A moved part is found again by its name; a deleted one is marked
+    **Missing** ("put it back in Movies/Phoenix, or tap Redo part") and the message names the part. Refresh marks such a part
+    Missing instead of removing it.
+  - Replaced, Lost and Missing entries do not keep a Space busy, and are not watched again at start.
+  - Redo part tapped twice on the same part does not start it twice.
+  - A failed merge says the parts differ (codec or size, e.g. made with different settings or Space versions).
+- **Checked here:** `SplitLogicTest.kt` (16 checks: a redone part completes the split, joined in order and once; another
+  unmerged split does not block it; merged, then a part redone: merged again under a new name; lost / missing parts hold the
+  merge and are named; History keeps an open split's parts past 50 and still drops the rest; 300 cap) - all pass with the real
+  Kotlin 2.0.21 compiler. All sources compile with no new error except references to Android types the sandbox has no
+  definitions for; the new file-check expressions were compiled and run against stand-ins for those types.
+- **Not checked here:** a Gradle / Android build and the app on a phone (the APK Builder is the real build).
+
